# Python Quality Standards

Global tooling (uv, ruff, ty, pytest) takes precedence over all project-level preferences.

## Tooling Commands

```bash
uv sync --locked --all-extras --dev
uv run ruff format .
uv run ruff check --fix .
uv run ty check .
uv run pytest
```

Both `ruff format` and `ruff check` must exit with code `0` before work is considered done.

---

## Docstrings

All public functions, methods, and classes must have NumPy-style docstrings.

Required sections (include only those that apply):

| Section | When to include |
|---------|----------------|
| `Parameters` | Function has one or more parameters |
| `Returns` | Function returns a non-`None` value |
| `Raises` | Function explicitly raises an exception |
| `Examples` | Non-trivial usage or public API |
| `Notes` | Important implementation details or caveats |

Private helpers (`_name`) may skip full docstrings but benefit from a brief one-liner.

---

## Type Hints

- All public function and method signatures must have complete type hints.
- Use built-in generics (`list[int]`, `dict[str, float]`) for Python ≥ 3.9.
- Prefer `X | None` over `Optional[X]` for Python ≥ 3.10.
- Do not use `from __future__ import annotations` for Python 3.11+ targets.

---

## Comments

- Comment only non-obvious logic, tricky flow, magic numbers, or algorithm steps.
- Do not restate what the code already says clearly.
- Imperative mood: "Clip to valid range", not "We clip to the valid range".

---

## Error Handling

- Do not wrap internal operations in `try/except` to suppress errors; let bugs surface.
- Validate inputs at system boundaries (CLI args, external files, user data), not between internal functions.
- Fail fast with a clear exception when a precondition is violated and continuing would produce silent wrong results.

---

## Formatting — `.py` files

Apply `uv run ruff format` and `uv run ruff check` before finishing any Python file.

## Formatting — `.ipynb` notebooks

Use `uv run ruff format` with notebook support enabled in `[tool.ruff]` (set `extend-include = ["*.ipynb"]`).

---

## Pre-submit Checklist

- [ ] Every public function/method/class has a NumPy-style docstring.
- [ ] Every public function/method has complete type hints.
- [ ] Comments only where logic is non-obvious.
- [ ] `uv run ruff format --check .` passes.
- [ ] `uv run ruff check .` passes (zero errors).
- [ ] `uv run ty check .` passes (or issues are acknowledged).
- [ ] No broad `try/except` hides internal bugs.
- [ ] Validation exists at system boundaries only.
- [ ] Any silent-wrong-result condition raises clearly.
